cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, the frozen weights, or the window index, please cite the accompanying article and this archive."
type: software
title: "ConvGRU NDVI Recovery: Code, Frozen Weights, Window Index and Result Tables"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ZhongGuoYoung/Recovery-of-Cropland-NDVI-Forecast-Accuracy-After-Satellite-Observation-Gaps"
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility archive for a study of how quickly cropland NDVI forecast
  accuracy recovers after satellite observation gaps. It contains the model and
  evaluation code, 36 frozen best checkpoints with SHA-256 inventory, the sealed
  matched-window index (11,315 paired windows) and its three-gap long form
  (33,945 rows), the audited Paper300 train/development manifests, and the
  derived result tables behind the letter's figures and tables. Training and
  replayed pixel arrays are not included; they are rebuilt from public inputs
  with the scripts and manifests provided.
keywords:
  - NDVI
  - ConvGRU
  - gap recovery
  - cropland
  - reproducibility
